  "name": "iroh",
  "description": "Iroh is a peer-to-peer networking stack designed for high-performance direct connectivity between nodes using public key-based addressing. It leverages the QUIC transport protocol to provide authenticated encryption and multiplexed streams, implementing robust NAT traversal through hole punching and globally distributed relay fallbacks. The framework facilitates decentralized application development by integrating discovery services, gossip overlays, and content-addressed data transfer within a unified connection management layer.",
